# m1_pool_threshold: return large blocks to the kernel instead of SEAL's free list. First step of the
# pool-first line, on m0_default; rule 4 against m0's peak table (383.9 GiB, 402,558,476 kB, re-freeze
# regime: zen4, 16-core cpuset, shared node, pmsample_chain).
#
# impl_lever: patch_pool_threshold.py
# impl_base_image: image:moai-cpu-m0_default.sif
#
# pool_attacked: host
# object_attacked: sealpool:retained
# object_skipped: keygenerator.h:208:seal::KeyGenerator::create_galois_keys(std::vector<int
# object_skipped: keygenerator.h:263:seal::KeyGenerator::create_galois_keys(seal::GaloisKeys&)
# cost_class: paid
# runtime_knob: yes
# evidence: exact
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# table      m0's peak (383.9 GiB; grouped by allocating function, share of attributed):
#              61.0 GB  14.8%  all_layer_test()  <- keygenerator.h:208:seal::KeyGenerator::create_galois_keys(std::vector<int, std::allocator
#              41.4 GB  10.0%  all_layer_test()  <- keygenerator.h:263:seal::KeyGenerator::create_galois_keys(seal::GaloisKeys&)
#              40.6 GB   9.9%  Bootstrapper::rotated_bsgs_linear_transform(seal::Ciphertext&, seal::Ciphertext&, int, int, int, std::vector<s
#              32.1 GB   7.8%  ct_pt_matrix_mul_wo_pre_large(vector<Ciphertext> const&, std::vector<std::vector<double, std::allocator<double
#              29.8 GB   7.2%  all_layer_test()  <- seal::Ciphertext::operator=(seal::Ciphertext const&)
#              29.4 GB   7.1%  batch_input(batch_input(...) [clone ._omp_fn.0]  <- seal::Encryptor::encrypt_internal(seal::Plaintext const&,
#              16.3 GB   4.0%  layernorm2(vector<Ciphertext> const&, std::vector<double, std::allocator<double> > const&, std::vector<double,
# position   pool-first decision (2026-08-29, re-examined 2026-09-21 against the chain-keyed m0 table).
#            Chain keys (pmsample_chain, 12 frames) name what sealpool:retained folded: key banks (61.0 GB
#            bootstrap, 41.4 GB attention), FFN intermediate, packed input and copy; all dead at m0's peak
#            (Layer-0 layernorm2/bootstrap4), held by the stock pool. Releases on the stock pool:
#            gelu_output_release +0.26%, x_copy_release -0.12%, boot_out_move +4.36%
#            (off-path-runs/m1_gelu_output_release, m2_x_copy_release, m1_boot_out_move), inside 0.53 pp.
#            minimal_att_keys acts on the stock pool (-5.2%, off-path.md) but less than the pool repair
#            (-26%); the pool repair enables m3..m6 and makes minimal_att_keys rank 1 with a free fix at
#            m1 (-20.7 GB there vs -20.9 GB on the stock pool). Both key rows declared skipped
#            (off-path.md, "Skipped at m0").
# mechanism  pool heads with item size >= threshold free on return; below: parent policy. 4 MiB catches
#            every ciphertext (21.7 MB at bootstrap output, 37.75 MB full level) and key element
#            (1,321,205,760 B). Compiled in; run records `LEVER|pool_threshold|bytes=4194304|source=compiled`.
# gate       bit-identical to m0 (md5 712aece2): the threshold pool changes the allocator, not the computation.
# RESULT (measured): peak 402,558,476 -> 298,290,352 kB (383.9 -> 284.5 GiB, -25.90%), wall 73,553 s, gate md5 712aece2.
# REFUTED IF the peak moves less than this system's run-to-run spread (0.53 pp), or the LEVER marker is absent from markers.txt.
